.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
node_modules/

# church data / enrichment CSVs live in the repo root while working;
# they are not part of the site
/*.csv

# One-off SQL also lives in the repo root while working -- probes, data
# corrections, and the generated hide/unhide lists an import leaves
# behind. Several say so in their own headers: event_categories_remap.sql
# opens with "Untracked on purpose (repo-root convention for one-off
# scripts)". Nothing enforced that, and on 2026-10-01 a working-tree
# snapshot swept 20 of them into a commit and pushed it here -- 4,238
# lines, of which 2,178 (find_missing.sql, unhide.sql) are literal lists
# of San Antonio church names and addresses. Same hazard as the CSVs
# above, for the same reason: Cloudflare Pages serves this root.
#
# Root-only by design. supabase/migrations/ and supabase/db-functions/
# are untouched -- SQL that is meant to be kept belongs there, not here.
# The few root .sql files already tracked stay tracked; this only stops
# the next untracked one from being swept up.
/*.sql

# Generated by tools/prep-texas.js. Not committed for the same reason
# as the root CSVs above, and one more: Cloudflare Pages serves this
# repo root, so committing them would publish ~15,000 church records as
# downloadable files on faithdock.com. Regenerate them instead.
/texas-batches/
/backups/
/churchfinder-batches/
/manual-adds/
/fss/
/faithstreet-batches/
